<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Prime Video Live Events Help Hub | Portfolio</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../../css/styles.css" />

  <style>
    /* ---------- Editorial Case Study (page-local styles) ---------- */

    :root{
      --ink:#111;
      --muted:#666;
      --border:#e9e9e9;
      --panel:#fafafa;
      --shadow: 0 14px 34px rgba(0,0,0,.06);
      --radius: 18px;
    }

    .caseWrap{
      max-width: 1120px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 64px 20px 96px;
    }

    .kicker{
      font-size: 12px;
      letter-spacing: .14em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }

    .title{
      font-size: 46px;
      line-height: 1.1;
      letter-spacing: -0.03em;
      margin: 0 0 14px;
      font-weight: 650;
      color: var(--ink);
    }

    @media (max-width: 680px){
      .title{ font-size: 34px; }
      .caseWrap{ padding-top: 44px; }
    }

    .dek{
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.75;
      color: #333;
      max-width: 78ch;
      margin: 0 0 22px;
    }

    .metaRow{
      display:flex;
      flex-wrap:wrap;
      gap:10px;
      margin: 12px 0 34px;
    }

    .chip{
      font-size: 12px;
      color:#555;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 999px;
      padding: 8px 10px;
      background: #fff;
    }

    /* Two-column layout */
    .grid{
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns: 2.2fr 1fr;
      gap: 40px;
      align-items:start;
    }
    @media (max-width: 940px){
      .grid{ grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; }
    }

    /* Main column */
    .main h2{
      font-size: 22px;
      margin: 44px 0 12px;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      color: var(--ink);
    }

    .main p{
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.9;
      color: #333;
      margin: 0 0 16px;
      max-width: 82ch;
    }

    .pull{
      border-left: 3px solid var(--ink);
      padding-left: 14px;
      margin: 26px 0;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: var(--ink);
    }

    /* Images */
    figure{
      margin: 34px 0;
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      overflow:hidden;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      background: var(--panel);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }
    figure img{
      width:100%;
      height:auto;
      display:block;
    }
    figcaption{
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--muted);
      padding: 12px 14px;
      background:#fff;
      border-top: 1px solid #efefef;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .twoUp{
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 18px;
      margin: 18px 0 6px;
    }
    @media (max-width: 760px){
      .twoUp{ grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }

    .miniGrid{
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 14px;
      margin: 18px 0 6px;
    }
    @media (max-width: 760px){
      .miniGrid{ grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }

    .divider{
      margin: 64px 0 0;
      border-top: 1px solid #eee;
    }

    /* Sidebar */
    .side{
      position: sticky;
      top: 24px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      padding: 22px;
      background: var(--panel);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }
    @media (max-width: 940px){
      .side{ position: static; }
    }

    .side h3{
      font-size: 13px;
      letter-spacing: .12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }

    .side ul{
      padding-left: 18px;
      margin: 0 0 18px;
      color:#333;
    }

    .side li{
      margin-bottom: 10px;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .side p{
      font-size: 14px;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }

    .callout{
      margin-top: 16px;
      padding: 14px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 14px;
      background: #fff;
      color:#333;
      font-size: 14px;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    /* Bottom nav */
    .navBottom{
      display:flex;
      justify-content:space-between;
      gap:16px;
      margin-top: 24px;
      flex-wrap:wrap;
    }
    .navBottom a{
      text-decoration:none;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 14px;
      padding: 12px 14px;
      background: #fff;
      color: var(--ink);
    }
    .navBottom a:hover{ background:#f7f7f7; }

    /* Optional: reveal-on-scroll (nice but subtle) */
    .reveal{ opacity:0; transform: translateY(10px); }
    .reveal.is-visible{ opacity:1; transform: translateY(0); transition: opacity .55s ease, transform .55s ease; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce){
      .reveal, .reveal.is-visible{ opacity:1; transform:none; transition:none; }
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>
  <header>
    <nav>
      <a href="../../index.html" class="logo">Shaazia</a>
      <ul class="nav-links">
        <li><a href="../../index.html">Home</a></li>
        <li><a href="../portfolio.html">Portfolio</a></li>
        <li><a href="../../index.html#contact">Contact</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main>
    <article class="caseWrap">
      <p class="kicker">Case Study</p>
      <h1 class="title">Prime Video Live Events Help Hub</h1>

      <p class="dek">
        A concept redesign of the Prime Video Live Events Help Hub—built to help customers get access,
        sign in, and resolve live streaming issues faster, while maintaining series branding (Thursday Night Football, NASCAR, and more).
      </p>

      <div class="metaRow">
        <span class="chip">UX Design</span>
        <span class="chip">Content Strategy</span>
        <span class="chip">Information Architecture</span>
        <span class="chip">Help & Support UX</span>
        <span class="chip">Live Streaming</span>
      </div>

      <div class="grid">

        <!-- MAIN COLUMN -->
        <div class="main">

          <h2 class="reveal">Context</h2>
          <p class="reveal">
            Live events are time-sensitive: customers often arrive minutes before a game or race begins,
            and they need immediate help with <strong>access, sign-in, device compatibility</strong>, and
            <strong>streaming performance</strong>. The Help Hub pages are branded per series, but the primary job-to-be-done
            is consistent: “Help me start watching (or fix what’s broken) quickly.”
          </p>

          <div class="pull reveal">
            The design goal: keep series branding, but make the experience feel unmistakably help-first—fast to scan,
            easy to act on, and aligned to customer mental models.
          </div>

          <h2 class="reveal">UX issues surfaced</h2>
          <p class="reveal">
            A review of the existing page structure surfaced several friction points that made it harder for customers
            to find the right action under pressure:
          </p>
          <p class="reveal">
            <strong>Mental model mismatches</strong>, lack of content chunking, distracting visual elements, choice overload,
            deceptive patterns, redundant links, and inconsistent content patterns across sections.
          </p>

          <h2 class="reveal">Help-first hierarchy</h2>
          <p class="reveal">
            The original experience leaned heavily into a promotional hero, which competed with the customer’s urgent goal.
            The redesign reframes the top of page to establish purpose quickly and route customers into “How to watch” immediately.
          </p>

          <div class="twoUp">
            <figure class="reveal">
              <img src="../../assets/images/PrimeVideoLiveEvents/before-hero.jpg" alt="Before: Live Events Help Hub hero with large branded treatment">
              <figcaption>
                Before: Branding dominates the entry experience, competing with task completion.
              </figcaption>
            </figure>

            <figure class="reveal">
              <img src="../../assets/images/PrimeVideoLiveEvents/after-hero.jpg" alt="After: Help-first hero with simplified hierarchy and clearer entry into how to watch">
              <figcaption>
                After: A help-first hero that quickly clarifies intent and directs customers into the primary task flow.
              </figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>

          <h2 class="reveal">Clear, predictable navigation</h2>
          <p class="reveal">
            Customers expect support pages to behave like support: clear sections, consistent labels, and fewer competing entry points.
            The redesign standardizes navigation around a task-based IA that matches user intent.
          </p>

          <div class="twoUp">
            <figure class="reveal">
              <img src="../../assets/images/PrimeVideoLiveEvents/before-navigation.jpg" alt="Before: Navigation and quick links create competing paths">
              <figcaption>
                Before: Competing “quick links” and section entry points increase decision load.
              </figcaption>
            </figure>

            <figure class="reveal">
              <img src="../../assets/images/PrimeVideoLiveEvents/after-navigation.jpg" alt="After: Simplified help hub navigation aligned to mental model">
              <figcaption>
                After: Simplified navigation aligned to “How to watch / Where to watch / Issues / FAQs / Get help.”
              </figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>

          <h2 class="reveal">Scannable chunking for “How to watch”</h2>
          <p class="reveal">
            “How to watch” is the critical path. The redesign condenses the flow into a single scannable module with clear steps:
            app download, sign-in/access, find the event, and take action (watch now / view schedule).
          </p>

          <div class="twoUp">
            <figure class="reveal">
              <img src="../../assets/images/PrimeVideoLiveEvents/before-how-to-watch.jpg" alt="Before: How to watch section with dense content and less clear hierarchy">
              <figcaption>
                Before: Key steps are present, but not optimized for fast scanning.
              </figcaption>
            </figure>

            <figure class="reveal">
              <img src="../../assets/images/PrimeVideoLiveEvents/after-how-to-watch.jpg" alt="After: How to watch module with clearer chunking and task-first actions">
              <figcaption>
                After: A single, scannable module that makes the path to watching obvious and fast.
              </figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>

          <h2 class="reveal">Reducing redundancy and choice overload</h2>
          <p class="reveal">
            The original page repeated links and pathways across sections, creating a “which one do I click?” problem.
            The redesign shifts to progressive disclosure: show the most common actions first, push edge cases deeper,
            and tighten CTAs so they read as support—not marketing.
          </p>

          <div class="twoUp">
            <figure class="reveal">
              <img src="../../assets/images/PrimeVideoLiveEvents/before-home.jpg" alt="Before: Full help hub page with dense sections and many repeated elements">
              <figcaption>
                Before: Dense page structure increases cognitive load and hides the fastest path to resolution.
              </figcaption>
            </figure>

            <figure class="reveal">
              <img src="../../assets/images/PrimeVideoLiveEvents/after-home.jpg" alt="After: Full help hub page with clearer sections and reduced repetition">
              <figcaption>
                After: Streamlined structure that surfaces common tasks first and reduces repeated links.
              </figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>

          <h2 class="reveal">Outcome</h2>
          <p class="reveal">
            This concept redesign establishes a scalable pattern for branded Live Events help pages:
            help-first hierarchy, consistent IA, scannable chunking for the critical path, and progressive disclosure
            for troubleshooting and FAQs—while keeping series identity intact.
          </p>

          <h2 class="reveal">How I’d measure success</h2>
          <p class="reveal">
            Increase engagement with “How to watch” actions, reduce pogo-sticking between sections,
            lower contact rate for common access questions, and improve time-to-resolution for sign-in,
            entitlement, and device compatibility issues.
          </p>

          <div class="divider"></div>

          <div class="navBottom">
            <a href="../portfolio.html">← Back to Portfolio</a>
            <a href="../../index.html#contact">Start a conversation →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SIDEBAR -->
        <aside class="side reveal">
          <h3>Project snapshot</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Product:</strong> Prime Video Live Events Help Hub</li>
            <li><strong>Context:</strong> Branded series pages (TNF, NASCAR, etc.)</li>
            <li><strong>Users:</strong> Customers trying to watch live events</li>
            <li><strong>Focus:</strong> Access, sign-in, streaming troubleshooting</li>
            <li><strong>Artifacts:</strong> IA, page structure, content modules</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 style="margin-top:18px;">Design themes</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Match customer mental models</li>
            <li>Chunk content for scanning</li>
            <li>Reduce choice overload</li>
            <li>Remove redundancy</li>
            <li>Make CTAs feel help-first</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="callout">
            <strong>What this redesign improves:</strong> A faster “start watching” path, clearer navigation,
            less decision fatigue, and a consistent support experience across branded live event series.
          </div>

          <div class="callout" style="margin-top:12px;">
            <strong>Key UX issues addressed:</strong> mental model mismatches, distracting visuals, deceptive patterns,
            redundant links, and inconsistent content structure.
          </div>
        </aside>

      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <p>&copy; 2026 Shaazia Stonehocker. All rights reserved.</p>
  </footer>

  <!-- Optional: reveal-on-scroll -->
  <script>
    (function () {
      const items = document.querySelectorAll(".reveal");
      if (!("IntersectionObserver" in window)) {
        items.forEach(el => el.classList.add("is-visible"));
        return;
      }
      const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
        entries.forEach(entry => {
          if (entry.isIntersecting) {
            entry.target.classList.add("is-visible");
            io.unobserve(entry.target);
          }
        });
      }, { threshold: 0.12 });
      items.forEach(el => io.observe(el));
    })();
  </script>
</body>
